    def __init__(self):
        pass

    def setup_oamops(self, **kwargs):
        """This keyword is used to Setup OAM operations for Primary BTS, currently using ADMIN and
        it also supports .
        If Remote LMP details exist in config data for given dut, it is considered as a chain setup.

        | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Comments* | *Config Ref* |
        | dut | bts |  Section Name in Testline Config  |  |
        | bts_host |  Default picked from TL config--><dut> | BTS's IP |  |
        | bts_port | Default picked from TL config--><dut> | BTS port |  |
        | user | Default picked from TL config--><dut> | ADMIN username |  |
        | password | Default picked from TL config--><dut> | ADMIN password |  |
        | use_ssl | True |  Use ssl |  |
        | update_interval | 5000 | Interval in (ms) to see updates from ADMIN API |  |
        | admin_api_log_dir | execution_logs | Path to store ADMIN API Log |  |
        | remote_lmp_ip | None | IP address of the remote LMP machine. If given under bts section in |  |
        |  | testline_config, this DUT is considered to be secondary BTS(Chained BTS scenario). |  |  |
        | timeout | 240 seconds | Timeout for connection |  |
        | alias | default | Name of the execution context |  |
        | cu_version | Default picked from TL config--><dut> |  cu version |  |


        *Examples:*

        *Setup OAM operations on bts with default values*
        | Setup Oamops |
        *Setup OAM operations on bts with explicit values*
        | Setup Oamops | bts_port=80 | use_ssl=False | timeout=120 | alias=conn1 |
        *Setup OAM operations on bts via mplane with explicit values*
        | Setup Oamops | bts_host=mplane | bts_port=80 | use_ssl=False | timeout=120 | alias=mplaneconn1 |
        *Setup OAM operations on chained bts*
        | Setup Oamops | dut=chained_bts1 | bts_port=80 | use_ssl=False | timeout=120 | alias=conn2 |

        *Examples:*

        *Setup OAM operations on bts with default values*
        | Setup Oamops |
        *Setup OAM operations on bts with explicit values*
        | Setup Oamops | jars_path=None | install_location=None |  host_ip=127.0.0.1 | log_path=/tmp |
        | timeout=None | ne=192.168.255.129 | pw=Nemuadmin:nemuuser | rc_only=False |

        """
        BaseClass().setup_oamops(**kwargs)

